source 'https://rubygems.org'

# This site is index.html (a redirect), manifest.json, site.webmanifest and a few
# images. Jekyll's only job is to copy them into _site: no page has front matter,
# so no layout is ever applied and nothing renders. Everything here is what that
# copy needs and no more.
gem 'jekyll', '~> 4.4'
gem 'webrick', '~> 1.8'

# github-pages used to be the only gem here, and it is why the dependency tree was
# stuck. It pins jekyll-remote-theme to 0.4.3, which requires rubyzip < 3.0, while
# rubyzip's path traversal advisory (GHSA-47m2-wp7j-p9vc) is fixed in 3.4.0. No
# amount of re-resolving could get past that, and github-pages has not had a
# release since August 2024, so the pin was never going to move.
#
# The pin was also doing nothing. remote_theme pointed at pages-themes/slate, but
# with no page carrying front matter there was no layout to apply and nothing ever
# used it. Dropping the meta-gem drops jekyll-remote-theme, and with it rubyzip, so
# the advisory goes away rather than being worked around.
#
# The cost is that jekyll moves from the 3.10.0 github-pages pinned to 4.4. That
# was unavoidable: 3.10 was only ever reachable through the meta-gem, and it was
# also what held activesupport and nokogiri below their security fixes.
